SOURCE IDENTIFICATION
=====================

The pin was verified on 2026-10-28 against the live PDF: 5801248 bytes,
223 pages, the December 2022 fourth-generation sentence present, no report
number in the file, and no contractor copyright reservation.

Systems Engineering for ITS, fourth generation, published December 2022.
Publisher: Federal Highway Administration, U.S. Department of Transportation,
Office of Operations (Systems Engineering for ITS resource). The document
combines and updates the FHWA Systems Engineering Guidebook (SEGB) and Systems
Engineering Handbook (SEHB) publications. The file carries no report number;
none is invented here. Source identified by title, publisher, and edition
only.

Reconstruction: all pack content is synthesized reference notes in the authors'
own words, drawn from the pinned document. The document itself is not
republished here; long verbatim passages are never reproduced, and no PDF
figures or page images are embedded.

NAMED-NOT-QUOTED MATERIAL
=========================

The following standards and bodies are identified by name in the source and in
this pack for reference only. They are copyrighted by their owners and are NOT
licensed to this pack. The pack restates only what the FHWA document itself
says about them. It reproduces no clause text, table, objective, or figure from
any of them:

-   INCOSE Systems Engineering Handbook, 4th Edition (International Council on
    Systems Engineering).
-   ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288:2015, System life cycle processes, and ISO/IEC/IEEE
    29148:2018, Requirements engineering.
-   NTCIP standards (National Transportation Communications for ITS Protocol)
    and SAE publications, named in the source's acronym list.
-   IEEE standards named in the source, including IEEE 1012-1998 (Independent
    Verification and Validation) and IEEE Std 1233 (System Requirements
    Specifications), and ANSI/AIAA-G-043-1992.
-   Any other third-party standard or publication named in the source.

Buy these from their publishers as applicable; see the se-standards-signpost
pack for the pointer table.

